difiers","level":"C1","prompt":"“A decision was made to measure the garden fence.” Which revision names the decision-maker clearly?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"The making of a decision to measure the garden fence occurred."},{"id":"B","text":"It was decided to measure the garden fence."},{"id":"C","text":"The committee decided to measure the garden fence."},{"id":"D","text":"A decision about the garden fence was made."}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Look for an explicit **actor as subject**, not just a noun naming the decision.","explanation":"The active verb and explicit subject **the committee** identify who made the decision.","keywords":["nominalisation-agent"],"skill":"nominalisation-agent","contextKey":"noun-modifiers-3","fingerprint":"e85c8491b61af8a95c175af956327ccd0b6f34bd3de78890f8eb2a7dc6ae4c00","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-noun-modifiers"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Look for an explicit **actor as subject**, not just a noun naming the decision.","The active verb and explicit subject **the committee** identify who made the decision.","Choose **The committee decided to measure the garden fence.**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The nominalised wording still hides the decision-maker.","B":"This impersonal passive also omits the decision-maker.","C":"The active verb and explicit subject **the committee** identify who made the decision.","D":"This still omits who made the decision."}}},{"id":"d401cedb-b779-5ddb-a448-ebd7cfaa8d23","topicSlug":"noun-modifiers","level":"C1","prompt":"Choose the modifier: “It is a ____ task to translate the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"5 hours''"},{"id":"B","text":"5-hourly"},{"id":"C","text":"5-hour"},{"id":"D","text":"5-hours"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Before a noun, build **number + singular unit** as 